  "description": "RIGYAJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C93 H119 Gd3 N2 O17 S8 Zn1,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.337-5.270 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.42-177.30°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C93H121N2O20S8ZnGd3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
